// Level maps for Ninja Master.
// Made by tools/genlevels.cjs. Run "node tools/genlevels.cjs" to make it again.
//
// Each level is a grid of letters. Every row must be the same length,
// and every level is 17 rows tall.
//
// The ground and the traps:
//   .  empty air        #  solid ground     =  platform (a thin plank)
//   ^  spikes (ouch)    ~  lava (ouch)      T  spring, it bounces you high
//   o  coin             P  where you start  F  the flag, touch it to win
//
// The baddies, two for each world:
//   Z  zombie, slow      S  skeleton, throws bones
//   W  snowman, throws snowballs             V  bat, it flies
//   U  mummy, slow and tough                 C  scorpion, fast
//   I  imp, it hops at you                   G  lava blob, jumps up and down
//   N  shadow ninja, throws darts            Y  ghost, goes through walls
//
// The bosses, one at the end of each world:
//   K  Skull King       J  Frost Giant      Q  Mummy Lord
//   D  Fire Dragon      X  Shadow Master
//
// Power ups you can pick up:
//   H  one heart back                        M  one more heart for ever
//   *  star power, for 8 seconds nothing can hurt you
//   B  jump boots, triple jump               R  rapid stars, throw much faster
//
// Rules that keep a level possible to finish:
//   1. Holes and lava are 3 columns wide or less. One jump goes about 4.
//   2. Spikes and walking baddies stay 3 columns away from a hole edge.
//   3. No platform sits above spikes or a walking baddy.
//   4. No platform hangs over a hole or over lava.
//   5. The floor never steps up or down more than 2 rows at a time.
//   6. A star only ever sits in the middle of a level.
//   7. Nothing at all sits next to the start, and nothing nasty next to the flag.
//
// There are 25 levels: 5 worlds with 5 levels each. The last level of
// every world is a boss fight, so it has a boss and no flag.

